  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate Proofed infrastructure - Rural roads in Arid and Semi-Arid Lands, Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project falls within the framework of the Common Programme Framework of the Ending Drought Emergency (EDE CPF) Pillar II - Climate-proofed Infrastructure of the Government of Kenya. The project aims to improve the transport network in 6 Arid and Semi-Arid Lands (ASAL) Counties of Kenya targeting a total estimated population of 1.5 million. The project will upgrade rural road infrastructure using labour based technologies with a focus on sustainability, provide training of small contractors, consultants, KeRRA and County officials on labour based technologies. The total project financing is EUR 112.5 million: EUR 60 million from AFD (credit), and EUR 30 million, from the EU AIP (grant) and expected contribution from the GoK counterpart of EUR 22.5 million. Kenya Rural Roads Authority (KeRRA) is the implementing agency.</narrative>
  </description>
